WEBVTT

00:00.421 --> 00:01.920
What we're going
to do in this video

00:01.920 --> 00:04.190
is study a proof of
the Pythagorean theorem

00:04.190 --> 00:07.590
that was first
discovered, or as far

00:07.590 --> 00:13.695
as we know first discovered,
by James Garfield in 1876,

00:13.695 --> 00:15.070
and what's exciting
about this is

00:15.070 --> 00:17.670
he was not a professional
mathematician.

00:17.670 --> 00:21.086
You might know James Garfield
as the 20th president

00:21.086 --> 00:21.960
of the United States.

00:21.960 --> 00:23.950
He was elected president.

00:23.950 --> 00:29.070
He was elected in 1880, and then
he became president in 1881.

00:29.070 --> 00:31.930
And he did this proof while
he was a sitting member

00:31.930 --> 00:33.889
of the United States
House of Representatives.

00:33.889 --> 00:35.264
And what's exciting
about that is

00:35.264 --> 00:38.390
that it shows that Abraham
Lincoln was not the only US

00:38.390 --> 00:41.330
politician or not the only
US President who was really

00:41.330 --> 00:43.280
into geometry.

00:43.280 --> 00:45.429
And what Garfield realized
is, if you construct

00:45.429 --> 00:46.970
a right triangle--
so I'm going to do

00:46.970 --> 00:49.310
my best attempt
to construct one.

00:49.310 --> 00:51.820
So let me construct
one right here.

00:51.820 --> 00:56.440
So let's say this side
right over here is length b.

00:56.440 --> 01:02.060
Let's say this side is
length a, and let's say

01:02.060 --> 01:05.269
that this side, the hypotenuse
of my right triangle,

01:05.269 --> 01:06.150
has length c.

01:06.150 --> 01:08.860
So I've just constructed
enough a right triangle,

01:08.860 --> 01:10.200
and let me make it clear.

01:10.200 --> 01:12.020
It is a right triangle.

01:12.020 --> 01:15.090
He essentially flipped and
rotated this right triangle

01:15.090 --> 01:18.750
to construct another one that
is congruent to the first one.

01:18.750 --> 01:19.900
So let me construct that.

01:19.900 --> 01:23.420
So we're going to have length b,
and it's collinear with length

01:23.420 --> 01:23.920
a.

01:23.920 --> 01:26.600
It's along the same
line, I should say.

01:26.600 --> 01:28.530
They don't overlap
with each other.

01:28.530 --> 01:33.070
So this is side of
length b, and then you

01:33.070 --> 01:35.340
have a side of
length-- let me draw

01:35.340 --> 01:39.460
a it so this will be a little
bit taller-- side of length b.

01:39.460 --> 01:44.210
And then, you have your side
of length a at a right angle.

01:44.210 --> 01:48.190
Your side of length a
comes in at a right angle.

01:48.190 --> 01:49.970
And then, you have
your side of length c.

01:56.232 --> 01:57.940
So the first thing we
need to think about

01:57.940 --> 02:01.190
is what's the angle
between these two sides?

02:01.190 --> 02:03.140
What's this mystery angle?

02:03.140 --> 02:06.787
What's that mystery
angle going to be?

02:06.787 --> 02:08.620
Well, it looks like
something, but let's see

02:08.620 --> 02:10.411
if we can prove to
ourselves that it really

02:10.411 --> 02:12.570
is what we think it looks like.

02:12.570 --> 02:15.340
If we look at this
original triangle

02:15.340 --> 02:18.030
and we call this
angle "theta," what's

02:18.030 --> 02:20.210
this angle over here,
the angle that's

02:20.210 --> 02:22.840
between sides of
length a and length c?

02:22.840 --> 02:26.000
What's the measure of
this angle going to be?

02:26.000 --> 02:28.650
Well, theta plus this
angle have to add up to 90.

02:28.650 --> 02:30.900
Because you add those two
together, they add up to 90.

02:30.900 --> 02:32.149
And then, you have another 90.

02:32.149 --> 02:35.080
You're going to get 180
degrees for the interior angles

02:35.080 --> 02:36.640
of this triangle.

02:36.640 --> 02:38.360
So these two have
to add up to 90.

02:38.360 --> 02:41.950
This angle is going
to be 90 minus theta.

02:41.950 --> 02:43.850
Well, if this triangle
appears congruent--

02:43.850 --> 02:46.110
and we've constructed
it so it is congruent--

02:46.110 --> 02:47.600
the corresponding
angle to this one

02:47.600 --> 02:48.850
is this angle right over here.

02:48.850 --> 02:51.430
So this is also going to be
theta, and this right over here

02:51.430 --> 02:53.385
is going to be 90 minus theta.

02:53.385 --> 02:54.760
So given that this
is theta, this

02:54.760 --> 02:57.550
is 90 minus theta, what
is our angle going to be?

02:57.550 --> 03:01.310
Well, they all collectively
go 180 degrees.

03:01.310 --> 03:05.010
So you have theta,
plus 90 minus theta,

03:05.010 --> 03:10.020
plus our mystery angle is going
to be equal to 180 degrees.

03:10.020 --> 03:12.770
The thetas cancel out.

03:12.770 --> 03:13.840
Theta minus theta.

03:13.840 --> 03:16.610
And you have 90 plus our
mystery angle is 180 degrees.

03:16.610 --> 03:19.840
Subtract 90 from
both sides, and you

03:19.840 --> 03:25.310
are left with your mystery
angle equaling 90 degrees.

03:25.310 --> 03:26.950
So that all worked out well.

03:26.950 --> 03:30.130
So let me make that
clear, and that's

03:30.130 --> 03:35.940
going to be useful
for us in a second.

03:35.940 --> 03:36.960
It's going to be useful.

03:36.960 --> 03:40.840
So we can now say definitively
that this is 90 degrees.

03:40.840 --> 03:43.260
This is a right angle.

03:43.260 --> 03:45.780
Now, what we are
going to do is we

03:45.780 --> 03:49.350
are going to
construct a trapezoid.

03:49.350 --> 03:52.490
This side a is parallel
to side b down here,

03:52.490 --> 03:55.190
the way it's been constructed,
and this is just one side right

03:55.190 --> 03:55.960
over here.

03:55.960 --> 03:58.760
This goes straight
up, and now let's just

03:58.760 --> 04:00.890
connect these two
sides right over there.

04:05.811 --> 04:07.310
So there's a couple
of ways to think

04:07.310 --> 04:10.940
about the area of
this trapezoid.

04:10.940 --> 04:13.090
One is we could just
think of it as a trapezoid

04:13.090 --> 04:15.970
and come up with its
area, and then we

04:15.970 --> 04:20.190
could think about it as the sum
of the areas of its components.

04:20.190 --> 04:23.900
So let's just first think
of it as a trapezoid

04:23.900 --> 04:26.410
so what do we know about
the area of a trapezoid?

04:26.410 --> 04:28.580
Well, the area of a
trapezoid is going

04:28.580 --> 04:31.590
to be the height of the
trapezoid, which is a plus b.

04:34.490 --> 04:36.930
That's the height
of the trapezoid.

04:36.930 --> 04:39.500
Times-- the way I
think of it-- the mean

04:39.500 --> 04:42.260
of the top and the
bottom, or the average

04:42.260 --> 04:43.405
of the top and the bottom.

04:45.990 --> 04:53.510
Since that's this times one
half times a plus a plus b.

04:59.239 --> 05:01.280
And the intuition there,
you're taking the height

05:01.280 --> 05:05.030
times the average of
this bottom and the top.

05:05.030 --> 05:07.530
The average of the
bottom and the top

05:07.530 --> 05:10.510
gives you the area
of the trapezoid.

05:10.510 --> 05:12.500
Now, how could we
also figure out

05:12.500 --> 05:15.260
the area with its
component parts?

05:15.260 --> 05:17.470
Regardless of how we
calculate the area, as long

05:17.470 --> 05:20.050
as we do correct things,
we should come up

05:20.050 --> 05:21.900
with the same result.

05:21.900 --> 05:24.260
So how else can we
come up with this area?

05:24.260 --> 05:30.170
Well, we could say it's the
area of the two right triangles.

05:30.170 --> 05:37.260
The area of each of them
is one half a times b,

05:37.260 --> 05:38.260
but there's two of them.

05:38.260 --> 05:41.160
Let me do that b in
that same blue color.

05:41.160 --> 05:43.500
But there's two of
these right triangle.

05:43.500 --> 05:45.710
So let's multiply by two.

05:45.710 --> 05:49.170
So two times one half ab.

05:49.170 --> 05:52.360
That takes into consideration
this bottom right triangle

05:52.360 --> 05:54.880
and this top one.

05:54.880 --> 05:57.400
And what's the area
of this large one

05:57.400 --> 06:01.150
that I will color in in green?

06:01.150 --> 06:04.200
What's the area
of this large one?

06:04.200 --> 06:05.920
Well, that's pretty
straightforward.

06:05.920 --> 06:07.800
It's just one half c times c.

06:07.800 --> 06:14.280
So plus one half c times c,
which is one half c squared.

06:14.280 --> 06:17.560
Now, let's simplify this thing
and see what we come up with,

06:17.560 --> 06:20.360
and you might guess where
all of this is going.

06:20.360 --> 06:22.520
So let's see what we get.

06:22.520 --> 06:25.680
So we can rearrange this.

06:25.680 --> 06:26.670
Let me rearrange this.

06:26.670 --> 06:36.370
So one half times
a plus b squared

06:36.370 --> 06:40.740
is going to be equal
to 2 times one half.

06:40.740 --> 06:42.280
Well, that's just
going to be one.

06:42.280 --> 06:48.855
So it's going to be equal
to a times b, plus one half

06:48.855 --> 06:49.355
c squared.

06:52.309 --> 06:54.350
Well, I don't like these
one halfs laying around,

06:54.350 --> 06:58.770
so let's multiply both
sides of this equation by 2.

06:58.770 --> 07:01.930
I'm just going to multiply both
sides of this equation by 2.

07:01.930 --> 07:05.386
On the left-hand side, I'm just
left with a plus b squared.

07:05.386 --> 07:06.260
So let me write that.

07:11.080 --> 07:14.395
And on the right-hand
side, I am left with 2ab.

07:19.340 --> 07:21.530
Trying to keep the
color coding right.

07:21.530 --> 07:23.220
And then, 2 times
one half c squared,

07:23.220 --> 07:27.250
that's just going to be
c squared plus c squared.

07:27.250 --> 07:28.870
Well, what happens
if you multiply out

07:28.870 --> 07:30.260
a plus b times a plus b?

07:30.260 --> 07:32.740
What is a plus b squared?

07:32.740 --> 07:45.590
Well, it's going to be a
squared plus 2ab plus 2ab plus b

07:45.590 --> 07:46.230
squared.

07:46.230 --> 07:51.080
And then, our
right-hand side it's

07:51.080 --> 07:52.930
going to be equal to
all of this business.

07:52.930 --> 07:56.390
And changing all the
colors is difficult for me,

07:56.390 --> 07:59.009
so let me copy and
let me paste it.

07:59.009 --> 08:01.300
So it's still going to be
equal to the right-hand side.

08:01.300 --> 08:03.440
Well, this is interesting.

08:03.440 --> 08:04.660
How can we simplify this?

08:04.660 --> 08:07.427
Is there anything that we
can subtract from both sides?

08:07.427 --> 08:08.260
Well, sure there is.

08:08.260 --> 08:09.790
You have a 2ab on
the left-hand side.

08:09.790 --> 08:11.373
You have a 2ab on
the right-hand side.

08:11.373 --> 08:14.830
Let's subtract 2ab
from both sides.

08:14.830 --> 08:19.650
If you subtract 2ab from both
sides, what are you left with?

08:19.650 --> 08:23.340
You are left with the
Pythagorean theorem.

08:23.340 --> 08:31.040
So you're left with a squared
plus b squared is equal

08:31.040 --> 08:33.120
to c squared.

08:33.120 --> 08:35.130
Very, very exciting.

08:35.130 --> 08:38.799
And for that, we have to
thank the 20th president

08:38.799 --> 08:42.919
of the United States,
James Garfield.

08:42.919 --> 08:44.890
This is really exciting.

08:44.890 --> 08:47.490
The Pythagorean theorem, it was
around for thousands of years

08:47.490 --> 08:49.160
before James
Garfield, and he was

08:49.160 --> 08:51.900
able to contribute just
kind of fiddling around

08:51.900 --> 08:55.206
while he was a member of the
US House of Representatives.
